      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "STATE IN TEXAS (3) saves his best form for this track and trip with four wins and two seconds from eight attempts and will be cherry-ripe now third run back from the break. Gets 2kg weight relief with the claim and is drawn to get all the favours from the inside alley. Plenty to like about his prospects. You'd love to own a stable full of gallopers like DIAMANTINA ROSE (5) who has only missed a drum once in 15 career outings. Never runs a bad race and has to be included in calculations. WONDEREACH (1) has had one run back from a break and was well held in sixth over 1000m at Sunshine Coast a month ago. Fitter and in the mix. PEWTER PEARL (8) is returning from a spell of four months. Finished fifth at Kembla Grange over 1000m at the first run last prep. Now with a new trainer Emma Fouchard and rounds out the selections in a competitive affair.",
